" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.1$ | $0.01$ | $0.04$ | $0.2$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.04$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.02$ | $0.04$ | $0.01$ | $0.2$ |\n\nCalculate $P(Y=2X)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-110964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y=2X) & =P(X=0,Y=0)+P(X=1,Y=2)+P(X=2,Y=4) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(1,2)+f(2,4) \\\\  & =0.1+0.2+0.2 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-110964" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a95abc9dbf1014f0fd42a2ebbc90e95e65ca663e6f022132972e58f996c7892"} {"question" "q-110964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-110964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0.14"] ["math" "0.3"] ["math" "0.32"] ["math" "0.4"] ["math" "0.5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-110964" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.5"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "|  | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | $Y=2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $0.15$ | $0.2$ | $0.06$ |\n| $X=1$ | $0.1$ | $0.2$ | $0.04$ |\n| $X=2$ | $0.05$ | $0.1$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0)$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X>1\\,\\,\\text{or}\\,\\,Y=0) & =P((X,Y)\\in {(0,0),(1,0),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2)}) \\\\  & =P((X,Y)=(0,0))+P((X,Y)=(1,0))+P((X,Y)=(2,0)) \\\\  & +P((X,Y)=(2,1))+P((X,Y)=(2,2)) \\\\  & =f(0,0)+f(1,0)+f(2,0)+f(2,1)+f(2,2) \\\\  & =0.15+0.1+0.05+0.1+0.1 \\\\  & =0.5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/state.json" "file_sha256" "e17b471c17cbc8d8b65a72e2e3eb3651d24fbc446c9937df7263b0c30d4d1d95"} {"question" "q-111081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14072641/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1a95abc9dbf1014f0fd42a2ebbc90e95e65ca663e6f022132972e58f